feat(ai): quality-first settings for public-facing content + fix the timeout ceiling

Measured with two new harnesses (ai:probe-thinking, ai:ab-content) rather than
inferred from docs. Three findings drove this:

1. THE 180s maxDuration WAS ALREADY UNSAFE. Long-form generations on the
   5-generation models measured 57-125s, and one config (sonnet-5 at xhigh
   effort) took 194s — over the routes' declared ceiling, which would 504 in
   production. draft also sets maxRetries: 4 against that same ceiling. Raised
   draft + guide-draft to 300s, Vercel's current per-function limit. This was a
   pre-existing fragility masked by Sonnet 4.6 being fast; it is not caused by
   the registry bump, but the bump would have exposed it.

2. ADAPTIVE THINKING SHARES THE OUTPUT BUDGET. The 5 generation runs adaptive
   thinking by default and its tokens come out of maxOutputTokens, so thinking
   competes with the article text. Measured: it declines to fire on most
   creative long-form (0 reasoning tokens in 7 of 8 runs) but consumed 57% of
   output on sonnet-5/xhigh, reaching 94% of the old 8000 ceiling. Combined with
   Sonnet 5 tokenizing ~30% heavier for the same prose, budgets were too tight:
   draft 8000 -> 12000, guide essay/howto 3800 -> 5700, guide 8000 -> 12000.
   Kept under 16000, above which non-streaming generateObject risks a timeout.

3. EFFORT IS A REAL LEVER AND WE WERE NOT USING IT. The pinned
   @ai-sdk/anthropic@3.0.99 exposes providerOptions.anthropic.effort, and it
   reaches the provider through the Gateway (verified: low=55, high=127,
   max=1008 reasoning tokens on the same prompt). Plumbed an optional `effort`
   through both wrappers and set it explicitly per lane:
   - long-form content (draft, guide-draft) -> 'high'. NOT 'xhigh': that is the
     config that blew the time budget on Sonnet 5 and hard-failed on Opus 5,
     for a modest word gain.
   - extraction + moderation (seo-meta, product-facts, suggest-links, moderate,
     comments) -> 'low'. 3x faster with no measured quality cost.

Model choice is deliberately NOT hardcoded here: Opus 5 for the content bucket
is AI_MODEL_CONTENT=anthropic/claude-opus-5, an operator env decision that keeps
its automatic Sonnet 5 failover. Opus 5 measured 30-40% more prose and better
brand voice than Sonnet 5 at ~2x cost.

Also adds scripts/ai-content-quality-ab.mjs + ai-thinking-probe.mjs so these
numbers can be re-derived when a model changes, and gitignores the generated
sample drafts.

135 tests green, tsc + eslint clean, full next build green.

